  "question": {
    "text": "A point on the parabola $y^2=18 x$ at which the ordinate increases at twice the rate of the abscissa is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "a5pJ7",
      "text": "\n$(2,4)$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "DpnDG",
      "text": "\n$(2,-4)$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "oEBxz",
      "text": "\n$\\left(\\frac{-9}{8}, \\frac{9}{2}\\right)$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "8Y28n",
      "text": "\n$\\left(\\frac{9}{8}, \\frac{9}{2}\\right)$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Any point be $\\left(\\frac{9}{2} t^2, 9 t\\right) ;$ differentiating $y^2=18 x$\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n& \\Rightarrow \\frac{\\mathrm{dy}}{\\mathrm{dx}}=\\frac{9}{\\mathrm{y}}=\\frac{1}{\\mathrm{t}}=2 \\text { (given) } \\Rightarrow \\mathrm{t}=\\frac{1}{2} . \\\\\n& \\Rightarrow \\text { Point is }\\left(\\frac{9}{8}, \\frac{9}{2}\\right)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$",
    "image": null
  },
